<main id="main" class="community-shell"><p class="eyebrow">API</p><h1>Community data, in JSON.</h1><p class="page-intro">Read server listings, ranked wins, match results and available replays. Public GET requests need no credentials. Server announcements require a provisioned server token.</p>
<section class="community-section"><h2>Public endpoints</h2><div class="data-panel table-scroll"><table class="community-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Action</th><th scope="col">Parameters</th><th scope="col">Returns</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach([['servers','format=text (optional)','Live server listings; text format supports native discovery'],['statistics','—','Community match and server totals'],['leaders','—','Up to 50 ranked winners, grouped by server and nickname'],['matches','server, mode, offset (optional)','Up to 50 matches; mode is all, ranked or casual'],['match','server, database, game','One match and its player statistics'],['player','server, nick','A server-scoped player’s latest 50 matches'],['replay','server, database, game; download=1 (optional)','Recorded replay events and integrity metadata']] as [$action,$parameters,$description]): ?><tr><td><code><?=site_h($action)?></code></td><td><?=site_h($parameters)?></td><td><?=site_h($description)?></td></tr><?php endforeach; ?></tbody></table></div><p>Use <code>/api/?action=ACTION</code>. Match offsets are 0, 50, 100 and so on. URL-encode parameter values. Server listings expire when operators stop reporting; rankings and replay evidence are server-reported.</p><p><a href="../?action=servers">Try server JSON →</a> · <a href="../?action=statistics">Try statistics JSON →</a></p></section>
<section class="community-section"><h2>Errors &amp; announcements</h2><p>Invalid requests return 400; failed server authentication returns 403; missing matches return 404; unsupported methods return 405; unavailable services return 503. Announcements use POST JSON with the provisioned server ID and token, and have a 2 MiB request limit. Keep tokens private and send them only over HTTPS.</p><p>Use the directory supervisor for announcements and durable match delivery. See the <a href="https://github.com/kladhest-se/lineclash/blob/main/docs/WEB-SERVICES.md">web-service integration guide</a>. The dedicated server’s separate status endpoint is documented in the <a href="https://github.com/kladhest-se/lineclash/blob/main/docs/API.md">server API reference</a>.</p></section></main><?php site_footer('../../'); ?>
